      "why": "Fully pipelined gives the highest Fmax and lowest latency per iteration, which helps meet the 0.44 us batch deadline for 32 simultaneous requests. Search lower W/N for area, with guards to ensure the 2^-12 error constraint is met."
    },
    {
      "family": "pipelined_m",
      "ranges": [
        {"param": "data_width", "low": 14, "high": 20, "choices": null},
        {"param": "n_iter", "low": 12, "high": 20, "choices": null},
        {"param": "angle_guard", "low": -2, "high": 2, "choices": null},
        {"param": "frac_guard", "low": 0, "high": 2, "choices": null},
        {"param": "rounding", "low": null, "high": null, "choices": ["trunc", "round"]},
        {"param": "m", "low": 2, "high": 8, "choices": null}
      ],
      "budget_share": 0.6,
      "why": "Registering every m stages reduces FF count and latency (ceil(N/m)+2), which can lower area and relax the Fmax needed for the batch deadline. The extra m parameter offers a richer area/latency trade-off; more budget is allocated to map it."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "Spec requires max_abs_err <= 2^-12 and 32 results within 0.44 us of a 1 MHz tick. Throughput >=32 Msps is trivial for 1 result/cycle, but the batch deadline demands Fmax >= ~73 MHz plus latency. Pipelined and pipelined_m both give 1 result/cycle. Accuracy depends only on W, N, guards, rounding, so we search W 14-20 and N 12-20 to cover the accuracy constraint with minimal area. Guards -2..2 and frac_guard 0..2 explore rounding/angle precision trade-offs. Pipelined_m's m 2..8 trades latency and FFs against Fmax. Budget split 40/60 to emphasize pipelined_m's larger parameter space while still mapping the fully pipelined front."
}

{
  "decision": "stop",
  "rationale": "This is the final round, and the front is feasible and well-covered, so no further exploration is possible. All three constraints are satisfiable: throughput_msps >= 32 (best seen 273, 0% violations), max_abs_err <= 0.000244141 (best 2.34e-05 = 2^-15.38), and sys_p99_batch_us <= 0.44 (best 0.165). The feasible Pareto front spans luts_plus_ffs 1144..2547 against HV ref 4000 and accuracy_bits 12.3..15.4 against HV ref 12, giving hypervolume 7272 with 26 unique feasible designs. The selection rule (min luts_plus_ffs) is served by the pipelined_m corner at luts_plus_ffs=1144, accuracy_bits=12.3, which still clears the error constraint (2^-12.35 <= 2^-12) and the system batch bound. No constraint is unreachable, so `infeasible` is not warranted; the front is good enough to stop."
  ,
  "next_plan": null
}
